{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfunv1sNbfAwgBkZ8uYuu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm not aware of an official, dedicated terminal chat client for Cloudflare Agents, so check the current Agents docs in case one has shipped. There are a few practical ways to do it:\n\n- **Write a small Node script** using `AgentClient` from `agents/client`. It's WebSocket-based (built on PartySocket) and lets you call the agent's methods and get its state from a terminal script.\n- **Connect directly to the WebSocket** with a generic tool like `wscat` or `websocat`. The default route is `wss://<your-worker>/agents/<agent-class-kebab>/<instance-name>`. You can also use `curl` if the agent handles HTTP via `onRequest`.\n- **Use an MCP client** if the agent is an `McpAgent`. Any MCP-capable CLI, including Claude Code (`claude mcp add --transport http ...`), can connect to it and use it from the terminal."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2244,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2244},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"755b5c81-9ab0-4488-963c-efe76c43cb90","uuid":"a51ab208-b66f-48e1-9e7c-6297a3bcf5ce","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:08:32.929Z","request_id":"req_011Cfunv1eUdQdp3xpfKgcCG"}
